# Copy to .env.local and fill in to enable real email login, cloud saves, and
# multiplayer rooms ("Play with friends" in Story).
#
# Without these, the game runs with a local dev fallback (email sign-in is faked,
# saves go to the browser's localStorage) and the friends panel shows a disabled
# notice. Solo play is identical either way. No code change needed to go live.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com
#   2. SQL editor → run supabase/schema.sql (PART A; PART B is a later step,
#      and the file says when)
#   3. Authentication → Providers → enable Email (magic link)
#   4. Authentication → URL Configuration → add http://localhost:3000 (and your prod URL)
#   5. Settings → API Keys → copy the Project URL and the publishable key
#
# NOTE ON THE KEY: Supabase replaced the legacy `anon` key with a publishable key
# (`sb_publishable_...`), and projects created since Nov 2025 have no anon key at
# all. The publishable key is a drop-in replacement — paste it below. The variable
# keeps its historical name; only the value's format changed. Never paste a
# `sb_secret_...` / service_role key here: NEXT_PUBLIC_* is shipped to browsers.
#
# NOTE FOR HOSTED DEPLOYS (Vercel etc.): NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined at BUILD
# time, not read at runtime. Adding or changing them in your host's dashboard does
# nothing until you trigger a fresh deploy.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Server-side score verification (optional, but it is what makes the ✓ real) ──
#
# With this set, a finished Story/Infinite run is posted to /api/submit-result,
# which REPLAYS the run from its recorded actions and derives the score itself
# before writing the row. The browser never sends a score. That is the difference
# between "Replayed" meaning something and it being decoration: without it, the
# thing computing the score and the thing vouching for it are the same program.
#
# Leave it unset and the game works exactly as before — runs post from the
# browser and simply never carry the flag. The route answers 503 and the client
# falls back on its own.
#
# THIS ONE IS SECRET. Supabase → Settings → API Keys → the `sb_secret_...` /
# service_role key. It bypasses every row-level-security policy in the database.
# Note the missing NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, and do not add one: NEXT_PUBLIC_* values
# are inlined into the JavaScript every visitor downloads, so prefixing this
# would publish the key that can rewrite anyone's data. It is read only by
# lib/supabaseAdmin.ts, which Next.js bundles into the server alone.
#
# On Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables. Then redeploy, then run
# PART B of supabase/schema.sql to close the browser's insert path for good.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
